  "solution": "Since \\(x^4+x^3+x^2+x+1\\) divides \\(x^5-1\\), we have\n\\[\nx^5 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{x^4+x^3+x^2+x+1}.\n\\]\nSo reduce the exponents modulo \\(5\\):\n\\[\n44\\equiv 4,\\quad 33\\equiv 3,\\quad 22\\equiv 2,\\quad 11\\equiv 1 \\pmod 5.\n\\]\nThus\n\\[\nx^{44}+x^{33}+x^{22}+x^{11}+1\n\\equiv x^4+x^3+x^2+x+1\n\\equiv 0\n\\pmod{x^4+x^3+x^2+x+1}.\n\\]\nTherefore the remainder is \\(0\\).\n\nThe answer is 0.",
